diff --git a/docs/examples.md b/docs/examples.md
index 2393dec..e207df0 100644
--- a/docs/examples.md
+++ b/docs/examples.md
@@ -497,6 +497,32 @@ This behavior can be changed using the *on_setattr* argument.
 
 Check out {ref}`converters` for more details.
 
+
+## Running Custom Code Before/After Setting Attributes
+
+The *on_setattr* hook can be a generator function that yields exactly once. Code
+before the `yield` runs with the incoming value, the yielded value is used as
+the value to set, and code after the `yield` runs with the new value already in
+place. The hook is still not run in `__init__`.
+
+```{doctest}
+>>> def gen_hook(instance, attrib, value):
+...     print(value)
+...     yield int(value) * 2 + 286
+...     print("set x to 420")
+>>> @define
+... class C:
+...     x: int = field(on_setattr=gen_hook)
+>>> c = C(42)
+>>> c.x
+42
+>>> c.x = "67"
+67
+set x to 420
+>>> c.x
+420
+```
+
 (metadata)=
 
